WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.990
In an ancient Hindu scripture, a father
teaches his son with salt and water.

2
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.210
Salt dissolves in water.

3
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:12.350
You can no longer see it, yet
it is everywhere in the water.

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.540
Something real can be present,
even when it cannot be seen.

5
00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.440
If you are not your
body and not your mind,

6
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.510
what are you, and where do you go next?

7
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.060
In this mission, you'll meet
three great Hindu thinkers,

8
00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:31.510
Shankara, Ramanuja and Madhva, who
answer that question very differently.

9
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.870
Then you'll see how these
beliefs shape daily life,

10
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.260
from food on the plate
to ideas about equality.

11
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:41.970
Your mission: find out
what you are, for Hindus,

12
00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.390
and where you go next.
